# Test case for the closed-loop heater path: klippy's PID drives the
# firmware's software-PWM heater pin, the bridge's thermal plant
# converts the duty into an evolving thermistor ADC value, and
# TEMPERATURE_WAIT gates on the measured temperature actually rising
# (then falling after the target is dropped). REQUIRES_EMULATOR: the
# assertions match klippy's periodic Stats lines, which only exist in
# real-MCU mode (fileoutput has no stats loop; it also bypasses
# TEMPERATURE_WAIT entirely, and there is no upstream fileoutput
# heater test, so nothing degrades on stock CI). The first assertion
# proves the plant heated into the wait window ([45,50] or the PID
# overshoot above it) while the target was 50; the second proves it
# decayed below 40 after the target was dropped to 0 - both are
# impossible without the full closed loop (PWM duty -> plant -> ADC ->
# PID) running.
CONFIG heater.cfg
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
EMULATOR heater.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "target=50 temp=(4[5-9]|5[0-9])\."
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "target=0 temp=(3[0-9])\."

M104 S50
TEMPERATURE_WAIT SENSOR=extruder MINIMUM=45

M104 S0
TEMPERATURE_WAIT SENSOR=extruder MAXIMUM=40

G4 P2000
